-- #1265, interface A: declares `Speak` with the default "A-default".  It has NO
-- import relationship with ifb.mdk, and their interface NAMES differ (`Speak` vs
-- `Greet`) -- the ONLY thing they share is the METHOD name `speak`.  That is the
-- discriminating variable: #1264 keyed the untagged-default registry by interface
-- IDENTITY, which separates two same-named interfaces but NOT two differently-named
-- ones sharing a method name at one dispatch tag.
export interface Speak x where
  speak : x -> String
  speak _ = "A-default"
